\id GEN Genesis 
\h Genesis 
\toc1 The First Book of Moses, called Genesis 
\toc2 Genesis 
\toc3 Gen 
\mt1 The First Book of Moses, called Genesis  
\c 1  
\p
\v 1 In the \w beginning|strong="H7225"\w* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w created|strong="H1254"\w* the \w heaven|strong="H8064"\w* \w and|strong="H0853"\w* the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w*.  
\v 2 And the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w* \w was|strong="H1961"\w* without \w form|strong="H8414"\w*, and \w void|strong="H0922"\w*; and \w darkness|strong="H2822"\w* \add was\add* upon the \w face|strong="H6440"\w* of the \w deep|strong="H8415"\w*. And the \w Spirit|strong="H7307"\w* of \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w moved|strong="H7363"\w* \w upon|strong="H5921"\w* the \w face|strong="H6440"\w* of the \w waters|strong="H4325"\w*.   
\p
\v 3 And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w said|strong="H0559"\w*, Let there \w be|strong="H1961"\w* \w light|strong="H0216"\w*: and there was \w light|strong="H0216"\w*.  
\v 4 And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w saw|strong="H7200"\w* the \w light|strong="H0216"\w*, \w that|strong="H3588"\w* \add it was\add* \w good|strong="H2896"\w*: and \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w divided|strong="H0914"\w* the \w light|strong="H0216"\w* \w from|strong="H0996"\w* the \w darkness|strong="H2822"\w*.\f + \fr 1.4 \ft the light from…: Heb. between the light and between the darkness\f*  
\v 5 And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w called|strong="H7121"\w* the \w light|strong="H0216"\w* \w Day|strong="H3117"\w*, and the \w darkness|strong="H2822"\w* he \w called|strong="H7121"\w* \w Night|strong="H3915"\w*. And the \w evening|strong="H6153"\w* and the \w morning|strong="H1242"\w* were the \w first|strong="H0259"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*.\f + \fr 1.5 \ft And the evening…: Heb. And the evening was, and the morning was etc.\f*   
\p
\v 6 ¶ And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w said|strong="H0559"\w*, Let there be a \w firmament|strong="H7549"\w* in the \w midst|strong="H8432"\w* of the \w waters|strong="H4325"\w*, and let it \w divide|strong="H0914"\w* the \w waters|strong="H4325"\w* from the \w waters|strong="H4325"\w*.\f + \fr 1.6 \ft firmament: Heb. expansion\f*  
\v 7 And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w made|strong="H6213"\w* the \w firmament|strong="H7549"\w*, and \w divided|strong="H0914"\w* the \w waters|strong="H4325"\w* \w which|strong="H0834"\w* \add were\add* \w under|strong="H8478"\w* the \w firmament|strong="H7549"\w* from the \w waters|strong="H4325"\w* \w which|strong="H0834"\w* \add were\add* \w above|strong="H5921"\w* the \w firmament|strong="H7549"\w*: and it was \w so|strong="H3651"\w*.  
\v 8 And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w called|strong="H7121"\w* the \w firmament|strong="H7549"\w* \w Heaven|strong="H8064"\w*. And the \w evening|strong="H6153"\w* and the \w morning|strong="H1242"\w* were the \w second|strong="H8145"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*.\f + \fr 1.8 \ft And the evening…: Heb. And the evening was, and the morning was etc.\f*   
\p
\v 9 ¶ And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w said|strong="H0559"\w*, Let the \w waters|strong="H4325"\w* under the \w heaven|strong="H8064"\w* be gathered \w together|strong="H6960"\w* \w unto|strong="H0413"\w* \w one|strong="H0259"\w* \w place|strong="H4725"\w*, and let the \w dry|strong="H3004"\w* \add land\add* \w appear|strong="H7200"\w*: and it was so.  
\v 10 And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w called|strong="H7121"\w* the \w dry|strong="H3004"\w* \add land\add* \w Earth|strong="H0776"\w*; and the gathering \w together|strong="H4723"\w* of the \w waters|strong="H4325"\w* \w called|strong="H7121"\w* he \w Seas|strong="H3220"\w*: and \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w saw|strong="H7200"\w* that \add it was\add* \w good|strong="H2896"\w*.  
\v 11 And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w said|strong="H0559"\w*, Let the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w* bring \w forth|strong="H1876"\w* \w grass|strong="H1877"\w*, the \w herb|strong="H6212"\w* \w yielding|strong="H2232"\w* \w seed|strong="H2233"\w*, \add and\add* the \w fruit|strong="H6529"\w* \w tree|strong="H6086"\w* \w yielding|strong="H6213"\w* \w fruit|strong="H6529"\w* after his \w kind|strong="H4327"\w*, \w whose|strong="H0834"\w* \w seed|strong="H2233"\w* \add is\add* in itself, upon the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w*: and it was so.\f + \fr 1.11 \ft grass: Heb. tender grass\f*  
\v 12 And the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w* brought \w forth|strong="H3318"\w* \w grass|strong="H1877"\w*, \add and\add* \w herb|strong="H6212"\w* \w yielding|strong="H2232"\w* \w seed|strong="H2233"\w* after his \w kind|strong="H4327"\w*, and the \w tree|strong="H6086"\w* \w yielding|strong="H6213"\w* \w fruit|strong="H6529"\w*, whose \w seed|strong="H2233"\w* \add was\add* in itself, after his \w kind|strong="H4327"\w*: and \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w saw|strong="H7200"\w* that \add it was\add* \w good|strong="H2896"\w*.  
\v 13 And the \w evening|strong="H6153"\w* and the \w morning|strong="H1242"\w* were the \w third|strong="H7992"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*.\f + \fr 1.13 \ft And the evening…: Heb. And the evening was, and the morning was etc.\f*   
\p
\v 14 ¶ And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w said|strong="H0559"\w*, Let there be \w lights|strong="H3974"\w* in the \w firmament|strong="H7549"\w* of the \w heaven|strong="H8064"\w* to \w divide|strong="H0914"\w* the \w day|strong="H3117"\w* from the \w night|strong="H3915"\w*; and let them be for \w signs|strong="H0226"\w*, and for \w seasons|strong="H4150"\w*, and for \w days|strong="H3117"\w*, and \w years|strong="H8141"\w*:\f + \fr 1.14 \ft the day…: Heb. between the day and between the night\f*  
\v 15 And let them be for \w lights|strong="H3974"\w* in the \w firmament|strong="H7549"\w* of the \w heaven|strong="H8064"\w* to give \w light|strong="H0215"\w* upon the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w*: and it was so.  
\v 16 And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w made|strong="H6213"\w* \w two|strong="H8147"\w* \w great|strong="H1419"\w* \w lights|strong="H3974"\w*; the \w greater|strong="H1419"\w* \w light|strong="H3974"\w* to \w rule|strong="H4475"\w* the \w day|strong="H3117"\w*, and the \w lesser|strong="H6996"\w* \w light|strong="H3974"\w* to \w rule|strong="H4475"\w* the \w night|strong="H3915"\w*: \add he made\add* the \w stars|strong="H3556"\w* also.\f + \fr 1.16 \ft to rule the day…: Heb. for the rule of the day, etc.\f*  
\v 17 And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w set|strong="H5414"\w* them in the \w firmament|strong="H7549"\w* of the \w heaven|strong="H8064"\w* to give \w light|strong="H0215"\w* upon the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w*,  
\v 18 And to \w rule|strong="H4910"\w* over the \w day|strong="H3117"\w* and over the \w night|strong="H3915"\w*, and to \w divide|strong="H0914"\w* the \w light|strong="H0216"\w* from the \w darkness|strong="H2822"\w*: and \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w saw|strong="H7200"\w* that \add it was\add* \w good|strong="H2896"\w*.  
\v 19 And the \w evening|strong="H6153"\w* and the \w morning|strong="H1242"\w* were the \w fourth|strong="H7243"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*.\f + \fr 1.19 \ft And the evening…: Heb. And the evening was, and the morning was etc.\f*   
\p
\v 20 And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w said|strong="H0559"\w*, Let the \w waters|strong="H4325"\w* bring forth \w abundantly|strong="H8317"\w* the moving \w creature|strong="H8318"\w* that \w hath|strong="H5315"\w* \w life|strong="H2416"\w*, and \w fowl|strong="H5775"\w* \add that\add* may \w fly|strong="H5774"\w* \w above|strong="H5921"\w* the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w* in the \w open|strong="H6440"\w* \w firmament|strong="H7549"\w* of \w heaven|strong="H8064"\w*.\f + \fr 1.20 \ft moving: or, creeping\f*\f + \fr 1.20 \ft life: Heb. soul\f*\f + \fr 1.20 \ft fowl…: Heb. let fowl fly\f*\f + \fr 1.20 \ft open…: Heb. face of the firmament of heaven\f*  
\v 21 And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w created|strong="H1254"\w* \w great|strong="H1419"\w* \w whales|strong="H8577"\w*, and every \w living|strong="H2416"\w* \w creature|strong="H5315"\w* that \w moveth|strong="H7430"\w*, which the \w waters|strong="H4325"\w* brought forth \w abundantly|strong="H8317"\w*, after their \w kind|strong="H4327"\w*, and every \w winged|strong="H3671"\w* \w fowl|strong="H5775"\w* after his \w kind|strong="H4327"\w*: and \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w saw|strong="H7200"\w* that \add it was\add* \w good|strong="H2896"\w*.  
\v 22 And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w blessed|strong="H1288"\w* them, \w saying|strong="H0559"\w*, Be \w fruitful|strong="H6509"\w*, and \w multiply|strong="H7235"\w*, and \w fill|strong="H4390"\w* the \w waters|strong="H4325"\w* in the \w seas|strong="H3220"\w*, and let \w fowl|strong="H5775"\w* \w multiply|strong="H7235"\w* in the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w*.  
\v 23 And the \w evening|strong="H6153"\w* and the \w morning|strong="H1242"\w* were the \w fifth|strong="H2549"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*.\f + \fr 1.23 \ft And the evening…: Heb. And the evening was, and the morning was etc.\f*   
\p
\v 24 ¶ And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w said|strong="H0559"\w*, Let the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w* bring \w forth|strong="H3318"\w* the \w living|strong="H2416"\w* \w creature|strong="H5315"\w* after his \w kind|strong="H4327"\w*, \w cattle|strong="H0929"\w*, and creeping \w thing|strong="H7431"\w*, and \w beast|strong="H2416"\w* of the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w* after his \w kind|strong="H4327"\w*: and it was so.  
\v 25 And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w made|strong="H6213"\w* the \w beast|strong="H2416"\w* of the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w* after his \w kind|strong="H4327"\w*, and \w cattle|strong="H0929"\w* after their \w kind|strong="H4327"\w*, and every thing that \w creepeth|strong="H7431"\w* upon the \w earth|strong="H0127"\w* after his \w kind|strong="H4327"\w*: and \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w saw|strong="H7200"\w* that \add it was\add* \w good|strong="H2896"\w*.   
\p
\v 26 ¶ And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w said|strong="H0559"\w*, Let us \w make|strong="H6213"\w* \w man|strong="H0120"\w* in our \w image|strong="H6754"\w*, after our \w likeness|strong="H1823"\w*: and let them have \w dominion|strong="H7287"\w* over the \w fish|strong="H1710"\w* of the \w sea|strong="H3220"\w*, and over the \w fowl|strong="H5775"\w* of the \w air|strong="H8064"\w*, and over the \w cattle|strong="H0929"\w*, and over all the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w*, and over every creeping \w thing|strong="H7431"\w* that \w creepeth|strong="H7430"\w* upon the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w*.  
\v 27 So \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w created|strong="H1254"\w* \w man|strong="H0120"\w* in his \add own\add* \w image|strong="H6754"\w*, in the \w image|strong="H6754"\w* of \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w created|strong="H1254"\w* he him; \w male|strong="H2145"\w* and \w female|strong="H5347"\w* \w created|strong="H1254"\w* he them.  
\v 28 And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w blessed|strong="H1288"\w* them, and \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w said|strong="H0559"\w* unto them, Be \w fruitful|strong="H6509"\w*, and \w multiply|strong="H7235"\w*, and \w replenish|strong="H4390"\w* the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w*, and subdue \w it|strong="H3533"\w*: and have \w dominion|strong="H7287"\w* over the \w fish|strong="H1710"\w* of the \w sea|strong="H3220"\w*, and over the \w fowl|strong="H5775"\w* of the \w air|strong="H8064"\w*, and over every living \w thing|strong="H2416"\w* that \w moveth|strong="H7430"\w* upon the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w*.\f + \fr 1.28 \ft moveth: Heb. creepeth\f*   
\p
\v 29 ¶ And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w said|strong="H0559"\w*, \w Behold|strong="H2009"\w*, I have \w given|strong="H5414"\w* you every \w herb|strong="H6212"\w* \w bearing|strong="H2232"\w* \w seed|strong="H2233"\w*, which \add is\add* upon the \w face|strong="H6440"\w* of all the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w*, and every \w tree|strong="H6086"\w*, in the which \add is\add* the \w fruit|strong="H6529"\w* of a \w tree|strong="H6086"\w* \w yielding|strong="H2232"\w* \w seed|strong="H2233"\w*; to you it shall \w be|strong="H1961"\w* for \w meat|strong="H0402"\w*.\f + \fr 1.29 \ft bearing…: Heb. seeding seed\f*\f + \fr 1.29 \ft yielding…: Heb. seeding seed\f*  
\v 30 And to every \w beast|strong="H2416"\w* of the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w*, and to every \w fowl|strong="H5775"\w* of the \w air|strong="H8064"\w*, and to every thing that \w creepeth|strong="H7430"\w* upon the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w*, wherein \add there is\add* \w life|strong="H2416"\w*, \add I have given\add* every \w green|strong="H3418"\w* \w herb|strong="H6212"\w* for \w meat|strong="H0402"\w*: and it was so.\f + \fr 1.30 \ft life: Heb. a living soul\f*  
\v 31 And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w saw|strong="H7200"\w* every thing \w that|strong="H0834"\w* he had \w made|strong="H6213"\w*, and, behold, \add it was\add* \w very|strong="H3966"\w* \w good|strong="H2896"\w*. And the \w evening|strong="H6153"\w* and the \w morning|strong="H1242"\w* were the \w sixth|strong="H8345"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*.\f + \fr 1.31 \ft And the evening…: Heb. And the evening was, and the morning was etc.\f*   
\c 2  
\p
\v 1 Thus the \w heavens|strong="H8064"\w* and the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w* were \w finished|strong="H3615"\w*, and all the host of \w them|strong="H6635"\w*.  
\v 2 And on the \w seventh|strong="H7637"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w ended|strong="H3615"\w* his \w work|strong="H4399"\w* which he had \w made|strong="H6213"\w*; and he \w rested|strong="H7673"\w* on the \w seventh|strong="H7637"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* from all his \w work|strong="H4399"\w* which he had \w made|strong="H6213"\w*.  
\v 3 And \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w blessed|strong="H1288"\w* the \w seventh|strong="H7637"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*, and \w sanctified|strong="H6942"\w* it: \w because|strong="H3588"\w* that in it he had \w rested|strong="H7673"\w* from all his \w work|strong="H4399"\w* which \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w created|strong="H1254"\w* and \w made|strong="H6213"\w*.\f + \fr 2.3 \ft created…: Heb. created to make\f*   
\p
\v 4 ¶ \w These|strong="H0428"\w* \add are\add* the \w generations|strong="H8435"\w* of the \w heavens|strong="H8064"\w* and of the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w* when they were \w created|strong="H1254"\w*, in the \w day|strong="H3117"\w* that the \nd \+w LORD|strong="H3068"\+w*\nd* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w made|strong="H6213"\w* the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w* and the \w heavens|strong="H8064"\w*,  
\v 5 And every \w plant|strong="H7880"\w* of the \w field|strong="H7704"\w* \w before|strong="H2962"\w* it was in the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w*, and every \w herb|strong="H6212"\w* of the \w field|strong="H7704"\w* \w before|strong="H2962"\w* it \w grew|strong="H6779"\w*: \w for|strong="H3588"\w* the \nd \+w LORD|strong="H3068"\+w*\nd* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* had \w not|strong="H3808"\w* caused it to \w rain|strong="H4305"\w* upon the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w*, and \add there was\add* \w not|strong="H0369"\w* a \w man|strong="H0120"\w* to \w till|strong="H5647"\w* the \w ground|strong="H0127"\w*.  
\v 6 But there went \w up|strong="H5927"\w* a \w mist|strong="H0108"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* the \w earth|strong="H0776"\w*, and \w watered|strong="H8248"\w* the whole \w face|strong="H6440"\w* of the \w ground|strong="H0127"\w*.\f + \fr 2.6 \ft there…: or, a mist which went up from, etc.\f*  
\v 7 And the \nd \+w LORD|strong="H3068"\+w*\nd* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w formed|strong="H3335"\w* \w man|strong="H0120"\w* \add of\add* the \w dust|strong="H6083"\w* \w of|strong="H4480"\w* the \w ground|strong="H0127"\w*, and \w breathed|strong="H5301"\w* into his \w nostrils|strong="H0639"\w* the \w breath|strong="H5397"\w* of \w life|strong="H2416"\w*; and \w man|strong="H0120"\w* became a \w living|strong="H2416"\w* \w soul|strong="H5315"\w*.\f + \fr 2.7 \ft of the dust…: Heb. dust of the ground\f*   
\p
\v 8 ¶ And the \nd \+w LORD|strong="H3068"\+w*\nd* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w planted|strong="H5193"\w* a \w garden|strong="H1588"\w* \w eastward|strong="H6924"\w* in \w Eden|strong="H5731"\w*; and \w there|strong="H8033"\w* he \w put|strong="H7760"\w* the \w man|strong="H0120"\w* \w whom|strong="H0834"\w* he had \w formed|strong="H3335"\w*.  
\v 9 And \w out|strong="H4480"\w* of the \w ground|strong="H0127"\w* \w made|strong="H6779"\w* the \nd \+w LORD|strong="H3068"\+w*\nd* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* to \w grow|strong="H6779"\w* every \w tree|strong="H6086"\w* that is \w pleasant|strong="H2530"\w* to the \w sight|strong="H4758"\w*, and \w good|strong="H2896"\w* for \w food|strong="H3978"\w*; the \w tree|strong="H6086"\w* of \w life|strong="H2416"\w* also in the \w midst|strong="H8432"\w* of the \w garden|strong="H1588"\w*, and the \w tree|strong="H6086"\w* of \w knowledge|strong="H1847"\w* of \w good|strong="H2896"\w* and \w evil|strong="H7451"\w*.  
\v 10 And a \w river|strong="H5104"\w* went \w out|strong="H3318"\w* of \w Eden|strong="H5731"\w* to \w water|strong="H8248"\w* the \w garden|strong="H1588"\w*; and from thence it was \w parted|strong="H6504"\w*, and became into \w four|strong="H0702"\w* \w heads|strong="H7218"\w*.  
\v 11 The \w name|strong="H8034"\w* of the \w first|strong="H0259"\w* \add is\add* \w Pison|strong="H6376"\w*: \w that|strong="H1931"\w* \add is\add* it which \w compasseth|strong="H5437"\w* the whole \w land|strong="H0776"\w* of \w Havilah|strong="H2341"\w*, \w where|strong="H0834"\w* \add there is\add* \w gold|strong="H2091"\w*;  
\v 12 And the \w gold|strong="H2091"\w* of \w that|strong="H1931"\w* \w land|strong="H0776"\w* \add is\add* \w good|strong="H2896"\w*: there \add is\add* \w bdellium|strong="H0916"\w* and the \w onyx|strong="H7718"\w* \w stone|strong="H0068"\w*.  
\v 13 And the \w name|strong="H8034"\w* of the \w second|strong="H8145"\w* \w river|strong="H5104"\w* \add is\add* \w Gihon|strong="H1521"\w*: the same \add is\add* it that \w compasseth|strong="H5437"\w* the whole \w land|strong="H0776"\w* of \w Ethiopia|strong="H3568"\w*.\f + \fr 2.13 \ft Ethiopia: Heb. Cush\f*  
\v 14 And the \w name|strong="H8034"\w* of the \w third|strong="H7992"\w* \w river|strong="H5104"\w* \add is\add* \w Hiddekel|strong="H2313"\w*: that \add is\add* it which goeth \w toward|strong="H1980"\w* the \w east|strong="H6926"\w* of \w Assyria|strong="H0804"\w*. And the \w fourth|strong="H7243"\w* \w river|strong="H5104"\w* \add is\add* \w Euphrates|strong="H6578"\w*.\f + \fr 2.14 \ft toward…: or, eastward to Assyria\f*  
\v 15 And the \nd \+w LORD|strong="H3068"\+w*\nd* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w took|strong="H3947"\w* the \w man|strong="H0120"\w*, and put \w him|strong="H3240"\w* into the \w garden|strong="H1588"\w* of \w Eden|strong="H5731"\w* to \w dress|strong="H5647"\w* it and to \w keep|strong="H8104"\w* it.\f + \fr 2.15 \ft the man: or, Adam\f*   
\p
\v 16 And the \nd \+w LORD|strong="H3068"\+w*\nd* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w commanded|strong="H6680"\w* the \w man|strong="H0120"\w*, \w saying|strong="H0559"\w*, Of every \w tree|strong="H6086"\w* of the \w garden|strong="H1588"\w* thou mayest \w freely|strong="H0398"\w* \w eat|strong="H0398"\w*:\f + \fr 2.16 \ft thou…: Heb. eating thou shalt eat\f*  
\v 17 But of the \w tree|strong="H6086"\w* of the \w knowledge|strong="H1847"\w* of \w good|strong="H2896"\w* and \w evil|strong="H7451"\w*, thou shalt not \w eat|strong="H0398"\w* of it: for in the \w day|strong="H3117"\w* that thou \w eatest|strong="H0398"\w* thereof thou shalt \w surely|strong="H4191"\w* \w die|strong="H4191"\w*.\f + \fr 2.17 \ft thou shalt surely…: Heb. dying thou shalt die\f*   
\p
\v 18 ¶ And the \nd \+w LORD|strong="H3068"\+w*\nd* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w said|strong="H0559"\w*, \add It is\add* not \w good|strong="H2896"\w* that the \w man|strong="H0120"\w* should \w be|strong="H1961"\w* alone; I will \w make|strong="H6213"\w* him an help \w meet|strong="H5828"\w* for him.\f + \fr 2.18 \ft meet…: Heb. as before him\f*  
\v 19 And out of the \w ground|strong="H0127"\w* the \nd \+w LORD|strong="H3068"\+w*\nd* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w formed|strong="H3335"\w* every \w beast|strong="H2416"\w* of the \w field|strong="H7704"\w*, and every \w fowl|strong="H5775"\w* of the \w air|strong="H8064"\w*; and \w brought|strong="H0935"\w* \add them\add* unto \w Adam|strong="H0120"\w* to \w see|strong="H7200"\w* what he would \w call|strong="H7121"\w* them: and whatsoever \w Adam|strong="H0120"\w* \w called|strong="H7121"\w* every \w living|strong="H2416"\w* \w creature|strong="H5315"\w*, \w that|strong="H1931"\w* \add was\add* the name \w thereof|strong="H8034"\w*.\f + \fr 2.19 \ft Adam: or, the man\f*  
\v 20 And \w Adam|strong="H0120"\w* \w gave|strong="H7121"\w* \w names|strong="H8034"\w* to all \w cattle|strong="H0929"\w*, and to the \w fowl|strong="H5775"\w* of the \w air|strong="H8064"\w*, and to every \w beast|strong="H2416"\w* of the \w field|strong="H7704"\w*; but for \w Adam|strong="H0120"\w* there was not \w found|strong="H4672"\w* an help \w meet|strong="H5828"\w* for him.\f + \fr 2.20 \ft gave: Heb. called\f*   
\p
\v 21 And the \nd \+w LORD|strong="H3068"\+w*\nd* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w caused|strong="H5307"\w* a deep \w sleep|strong="H8639"\w* to \w fall|strong="H5307"\w* upon \w Adam|strong="H0121"\w*, and he \w slept|strong="H3462"\w*: and he \w took|strong="H3947"\w* \w one|strong="H0259"\w* of his \w ribs|strong="H6763"\w*, and closed \w up|strong="H5462"\w* the \w flesh|strong="H1320"\w* instead thereof;  
\v 22 And the \w rib|strong="H6763"\w*, which the \nd \+w LORD|strong="H3068"\+w*\nd* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* had \w taken|strong="H3947"\w* from \w man|strong="H0120"\w*, \w made|strong="H1129"\w* he a \w woman|strong="H0802"\w*, and \w brought|strong="H0935"\w* her unto the \w man|strong="H0120"\w*.\f + \fr 2.22 \ft made: Heb. builded\f*  
\v 23 And \w Adam|strong="H0120"\w* \w said|strong="H0559"\w*, \w This|strong="H2063"\w* \add is\add* \w now|strong="H6471"\w* \w bone|strong="H6106"\w* of my \w bones|strong="H6106"\w*, and \w flesh|strong="H1320"\w* of my \w flesh|strong="H1320"\w*: \w she|strong="H2063"\w* shall be \w called|strong="H7121"\w* \w Woman|strong="H0802"\w*, because \w she|strong="H2063"\w* was \w taken|strong="H3947"\w* out of \w Man|strong="H0376"\w*.\f + \fr 2.23 \ft Woman: Heb. Isha\f*\f + \fr 2.23 \ft Man: Heb. Ish\f*  
\v 24 \w Therefore|strong="H3651"\w* shall a \w man|strong="H0376"\w* \w leave|strong="H5800"\w* his \w father|strong="H0001"\w* and his \w mother|strong="H0517"\w*, and shall \w cleave|strong="H1692"\w* unto his \w wife|strong="H0802"\w*: and they shall be \w one|strong="H0259"\w* \w flesh|strong="H1320"\w*.  
\v 25 And they were \w both|strong="H8147"\w* \w naked|strong="H6174"\w*, the \w man|strong="H0120"\w* and his \w wife|strong="H0802"\w*, and were not \w ashamed|strong="H0954"\w*.   
\c 3  
\p
\v 1 Now the \w serpent|strong="H5175"\w* \w was|strong="H1961"\w* more \w subtil|strong="H6175"\w* than any \w beast|strong="H2416"\w* of the \w field|strong="H7704"\w* which the \nd \+w LORD|strong="H3068"\+w*\nd* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* had \w made|strong="H6213"\w*. And he \w said|strong="H0559"\w* unto the \w woman|strong="H0802"\w*, \w Yea|strong="H0637"\w*, hath \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w said|strong="H0559"\w*, Ye shall not \w eat|strong="H0398"\w* of every \w tree|strong="H6086"\w* of the \w garden|strong="H1588"\w*?\f + \fr 3.1 \ft Yea…: Heb. Yea, because, etc.\f*  
\v 2 And the \w woman|strong="H0802"\w* \w said|strong="H0559"\w* unto the \w serpent|strong="H5175"\w*, We may \w eat|strong="H0398"\w* of the \w fruit|strong="H6529"\w* of the \w trees|strong="H6086"\w* of the \w garden|strong="H1588"\w*:  
\v 3 But of the \w fruit|strong="H6529"\w* of the \w tree|strong="H6086"\w* which \add is\add* in the \w midst|strong="H8432"\w* of the \w garden|strong="H1588"\w*, \w God|strong="H0430"\w* hath \w said|strong="H0559"\w*, Ye shall not \w eat|strong="H0398"\w* of it, neither shall ye \w touch|strong="H5060"\w* it, \w lest|strong="H6435"\w* ye \w die|strong="H4191"\w*.  
\v 4 And the \w serpent|strong="H5175"\w* \w said|strong="H0559"\w* unto the \w woman|strong="H0802"\w*, Ye shall not \w surely|strong="H4191"\w* \w die|strong="H4191"\w*:  
\v 5 For \w God|strong="H0430"\w* doth \w know|strong="H3045"\w* that in the \w day|strong="H3117"\w* ye \w eat|strong="H0398"\w* thereof, then your \w eyes|strong="H5869"\w* shall be \w opened|strong="H6491"\w*, and ye shall be as \w gods|strong="H0430"\w*, \w knowing|strong="H3045"\w* \w good|strong="H2896"\w* and \w evil|strong="H7451"\w*.   
\p
\v 6 And when the \w woman|strong="H0802"\w* \w saw|strong="H7200"\w* that the \w tree|strong="H6086"\w* \add was\add* \w good|strong="H2896"\w* for \w food|strong="H3978"\w*, and that \w it|strong="H1931"\w* \add was\add* \w pleasant|strong="H8378"\w* to the \w eyes|strong="H5869"\w*, and a \w tree|strong="H6086"\w* to be \w desired|strong="H2530"\w* to make \add one\add* \w wise|strong="H7919"\w*, she \w took|strong="H3947"\w* of the fruit \w thereof|strong="H6529"\w*, and did \w eat|strong="H0398"\w*, and \w gave|strong="H5414"\w* \w also|strong="H1571"\w* unto her \w husband|strong="H0376"\w* with her; and he did \w eat|strong="H0398"\w*.\f + \fr 3.6 \ft pleasant: Heb. a desire\f*  
\v 7 And the \w eyes|strong="H5869"\w* of them \w both|strong="H8147"\w* were \w opened|strong="H6491"\w*, and \w they|strong="H1992"\w* \w knew|strong="H3045"\w* that they \add were\add* \w naked|strong="H5903"\w*; and they \w sewed|strong="H8609"\w* \w fig|strong="H8384"\w* \w leaves|strong="H5929"\w* \w together|strong="H8609"\w*, and made \w themselves|strong="H6213"\w* \w aprons|strong="H2290"\w*.\f + \fr 3.7 \ft aprons: or, things to gird about\f*  
\v 8 And they \w heard|strong="H8085"\w* the \w voice|strong="H6963"\w* of the \nd \+w LORD|strong="H3068"\+w*\nd* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w walking|strong="H1980"\w* in the \w garden|strong="H1588"\w* in the \w cool|strong="H7307"\w* of the \w day|strong="H3117"\w*: and \w Adam|strong="H0120"\w* and his \w wife|strong="H0802"\w* hid \w themselves|strong="H2244"\w* from the \w presence|strong="H6440"\w* of the \nd \+w LORD|strong="H3068"\+w*\nd* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w amongst|strong="H8432"\w* the \w trees|strong="H6086"\w* of the \w garden|strong="H1588"\w*.\f + \fr 3.8 \ft cool: Heb. wind\f*   
\p
\v 9 And the \nd \+w LORD|strong="H3068"\+w*\nd* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w called|strong="H7121"\w* unto \w Adam|strong="H0120"\w*, and \w said|strong="H0559"\w* unto him, Where \add art\add* \w thou|strong="H0335"\w*?  
\v 10 And he \w said|strong="H0559"\w*, I \w heard|strong="H8085"\w* thy \w voice|strong="H6963"\w* in the \w garden|strong="H1588"\w*, and I was \w afraid|strong="H3372"\w*, because \w I|strong="H0595"\w* \add was\add* \w naked|strong="H5903"\w*; and I hid \w myself|strong="H2244"\w*.   
\p
\v 11 And he \w said|strong="H0559"\w*, \w Who|strong="H4310"\w* \w told|strong="H5046"\w* thee that thou \add wast\add* \w naked|strong="H5903"\w*? Hast thou \w eaten|strong="H0398"\w* of the \w tree|strong="H6086"\w*, whereof I commanded \w thee|strong="H6680"\w* that thou shouldest \w not|strong="H1115"\w* \w eat|strong="H0398"\w*?  
\v 12 And the \w man|strong="H0120"\w* \w said|strong="H0559"\w*, The \w woman|strong="H0802"\w* whom thou \w gavest|strong="H5414"\w* \add to be\add* with \w me|strong="H5978"\w*, \w she|strong="H1931"\w* \w gave|strong="H5414"\w* me of the \w tree|strong="H6086"\w*, and I did \w eat|strong="H0398"\w*.  
\v 13 And the \nd \+w LORD|strong="H3068"\+w*\nd* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w said|strong="H0559"\w* unto the \w woman|strong="H0802"\w*, What \add is\add* this \add that\add* thou hast \w done|strong="H6213"\w*? And the \w woman|strong="H0802"\w* \w said|strong="H0559"\w*, The \w serpent|strong="H5175"\w* beguiled \w me|strong="H5377"\w*, and I did \w eat|strong="H0398"\w*.   
\p
\v 14 And the \nd \+w LORD|strong="H3068"\+w*\nd* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w said|strong="H0559"\w* unto the \w serpent|strong="H5175"\w*, Because \w thou|strong="H0859"\w* hast \w done|strong="H6213"\w* this, thou \add art\add* \w cursed|strong="H0779"\w* above all \w cattle|strong="H0929"\w*, and above every \w beast|strong="H2416"\w* of the \w field|strong="H7704"\w*; upon thy \w belly|strong="H1512"\w* shalt thou \w go|strong="H3212"\w*, and \w dust|strong="H6083"\w* shalt thou \w eat|strong="H0398"\w* all the \w days|strong="H3117"\w* of thy \w life|strong="H2416"\w*:  
\v 15 And I will \w put|strong="H7896"\w* \w enmity|strong="H0342"\w* between thee and the \w woman|strong="H0802"\w*, and between thy \w seed|strong="H2233"\w* and her \w seed|strong="H2233"\w*; it shall \w bruise|strong="H7779"\w* thy \w head|strong="H7218"\w*, and thou shalt \w bruise|strong="H7779"\w* his \w heel|strong="H6119"\w*.  
\v 16 Unto the \w woman|strong="H0802"\w* he \w said|strong="H0559"\w*, I will \w greatly|strong="H7235"\w* \w multiply|strong="H7235"\w* thy \w sorrow|strong="H6093"\w* and thy \w conception|strong="H2032"\w*; in \w sorrow|strong="H6089"\w* thou shalt bring \w forth|strong="H3205"\w* \w children|strong="H1121"\w*; and thy \w desire|strong="H8669"\w* \add shall be\add* to thy \w husband|strong="H0376"\w*, and he shall \w rule|strong="H4910"\w* over thee.\f + \fr 3.16 \ft to thy…: or, subject to thy husband\f*   
\p
\v 17 And unto \w Adam|strong="H0121"\w* he \w said|strong="H0559"\w*, Because thou hast \w hearkened|strong="H8085"\w* unto the \w voice|strong="H6963"\w* of thy \w wife|strong="H0802"\w*, and hast \w eaten|strong="H0398"\w* of the \w tree|strong="H6086"\w*, of \w which|strong="H0834"\w* I commanded \w thee|strong="H6680"\w*, \w saying|strong="H0559"\w*, Thou shalt not \w eat|strong="H0398"\w* of it: \w cursed|strong="H0779"\w* \add is\add* the \w ground|strong="H0127"\w* for thy sake; in \w sorrow|strong="H6093"\w* shalt thou \w eat|strong="H0398"\w* \add of\add* it \w all|strong="H3605"\w* the \w days|strong="H3117"\w* of thy \w life|strong="H2416"\w*;  
\v 18 Thorns \w also|strong="H6975"\w* and \w thistles|strong="H1863"\w* shall it bring \w forth|strong="H6779"\w* to thee; and thou shalt \w eat|strong="H0398"\w* the \w herb|strong="H6212"\w* of the \w field|strong="H7704"\w*;\f + \fr 3.18 \ft bring…: Heb. cause to bud\f*  
\v 19 In the \w sweat|strong="H2188"\w* of thy \w face|strong="H0639"\w* shalt thou \w eat|strong="H0398"\w* \w bread|strong="H3899"\w*, \w till|strong="H5704"\w* thou \w return|strong="H7725"\w* unto the \w ground|strong="H0127"\w*; for out of it wast thou \w taken|strong="H3947"\w*: for \w dust|strong="H6083"\w* \w thou|strong="H0859"\w* \add art\add*, and unto \w dust|strong="H6083"\w* shalt thou \w return|strong="H7725"\w*.  
\v 20 And \w Adam|strong="H0120"\w* \w called|strong="H7121"\w* his \w wife’s|strong="H0802"\w* \w name|strong="H8034"\w* \w Eve|strong="H2332"\w*; because she was the \w mother|strong="H0517"\w* of all \w living|strong="H2416"\w*.\f + \fr 3.20 \ft Eve: Heb. Chavah: that is Living\f*  
\v 21 Unto \w Adam|strong="H0120"\w* also and to his \w wife|strong="H0802"\w* did the \nd \+w LORD|strong="H3068"\+w*\nd* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w make|strong="H6213"\w* \w coats|strong="H3801"\w* of \w skins|strong="H5785"\w*, and clothed \w them|strong="H3847"\w*.   
\p
\v 22 ¶ And the \nd \+w LORD|strong="H3068"\+w*\nd* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* \w said|strong="H0559"\w*, \w Behold|strong="H2005"\w*, the \w man|strong="H0120"\w* is become as \w one|strong="H0259"\w* of us, to \w know|strong="H3045"\w* \w good|strong="H2896"\w* and \w evil|strong="H7451"\w*: and now, lest he put \w forth|strong="H7971"\w* his \w hand|strong="H3027"\w*, and \w take|strong="H3947"\w* also of the \w tree|strong="H6086"\w* of \w life|strong="H2416"\w*, and \w eat|strong="H0398"\w*, and \w live|strong="H2425"\w* for \w ever|strong="H5769"\w*:  
\v 23 Therefore the \nd \+w LORD|strong="H3068"\+w*\nd* \w God|strong="H0430"\w* sent him \w forth|strong="H7971"\w* from the \w garden|strong="H1588"\w* of \w Eden|strong="H5731"\w*, to \w till|strong="H5647"\w* the \w ground|strong="H0127"\w* from whence he was \w taken|strong="H3947"\w*.  
\v 24 So he drove \w out|strong="H1644"\w* the \w man|strong="H0120"\w*; and he \w placed|strong="H7931"\w* at the \w east|strong="H6924"\w* of the \w garden|strong="H1588"\w* of \w Eden|strong="H5731"\w* \w Cherubims|strong="H3742"\w*, and a \w flaming|strong="H3858"\w* \w sword|strong="H2719"\w* which turned every \w way|strong="H2015"\w*, to \w keep|strong="H8104"\w* the \w way|strong="H1870"\w* of the \w tree|strong="H6086"\w* of \w life|strong="H2416"\w*.   
